From 8f662c996a73d3e38556c60ffad8512c295217e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:37:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] arm64: nexell: minimal S5P6818 platform bring-up (console
 + SD)

Mainline has never carried the Nexell S5PXX18 (S5P6818) platform. This
adds a minimal, from-scratch bring-up sufficient to boot to a serial
console and access SD/eMMC using only generic drivers:

  * ARCH_NEXELL platform Kconfig + arm64 dts subdir
  * s5p6818.dtsi / s5p6818-nanopi-m3.dts: single-core (secondaries need
    PSCI/SMP glue, later), GIC-400, ARM arch timer, fixed-rate clocks
    (SoC PLLs left as configured by u-boot), samsung,s5pv210-uart console
    and a generic snps,dw-mshc SD controller. Pin muxing is inherited
    from u-boot for now.
  * samsung_tty: the S5P6818 UART is register-compatible with S5PV210, so
    reuse s5pv210 drvdata on ARCH_NEXELL (CONFIG_CPU_S5PV210 is 32-bit
    only) and allow SERIAL_SAMSUNG to be selected on ARCH_NEXELL.

SoC-specific clk/pinctrl/reset drivers, SMP and the remaining peripherals
are added in follow-up stages. GPU/VPU/display are out of scope.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
